{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-317590b3-7fdc-401e-83d2-11e948488e87","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JMuedTF7sTkh6WrDhRcJSf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/ziming/kda-ops/kda-runs/formal-kda-h100-20260920--flashinfer--rmsnorm_h4096/docs/plan.md","old_string":"**Next step (separate turn):** implement `solution/solution.py` for **c001** only, run the\nstatic checklist, then evaluate. No other candidate until c001's record is appended.","new_string":"**Next step (separate turn):** implement `solution/solution.py` for **c001** only, run the\nstatic checklist, then evaluate. No other candidate until c001's record is appended.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Decision log (append-only)\n\n- **c001 (eval #1) — accept-as-best. geomean 4.10x, 14/14 pass.** Device confirmed:\n  **NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3** (not A800 — portable memory-bound design was the right call).\n  Tolerance: atol=0.01, rtol=0.01, matched_ratio=0.99. Fused baseline validated the whole\n  numerical approach (max rel err 7.81e-3, well inside tol). Regime split as predicted:\n  small batches 1–170 ≈ **2.38–2.70x** (launch/latency-bound, dominate 9/14 of the\n  geomean); large batches 8804–14509 ≈ **8.88–9.73x** (bandwidth-bound). Small-batch\n  sol times are ~0.029–0.036 ms and nearly flat across batch 1→170 → almost pure fixed\n  overhead (launch + kernel prologue), not compute. **Next lever = c002/c003 num_warps\n  sweep** (H2): fewer warps (e.g. 4) may cut per-row prologue/latency on the tiny batches\n  that dominate the geomean; will branch from c001 changing only `num_warps`. Large-batch\n  amortization (c004) is secondary since it only moves 5/14 factors."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcb7278b-5119-4225-84cc-a12fe